// Lesson 2 — 7
::U5FINAL L2Q1::A communicable disease is one that {=can spread through infectious transmission ~is always chronic ~is caused only by behavior ~cannot be prevented}

::U5FINAL L2Q2::A pathogen is {=a disease-causing organism or agent ~a protective behavior ~a screening result ~an access barrier}

::U5FINAL L2Q3::Which action interrupts respiratory transmission? {=Appropriate ventilation and staying away from others when ill ~Sharing drinks ~Ignoring symptoms ~Touching the face after exposure}

::U5FINAL L2Q4::Exposure means {=contact with a possible source, not proof of infection ~confirmed diagnosis ~guaranteed symptoms ~completed treatment}

::U5FINAL L2Q5::Symptoms alone {=may suggest a need for evaluation but do not always establish diagnosis ~always identify the exact pathogen ~prove who caused infection ~replace testing}

::U5FINAL L2Q6::Which is a community prevention strategy? {=A vaccination or public-health education program ~Sharing misinformation ~Discouraging testing ~Hiding outbreak information}

::U5FINAL L2Q7::After a fictional possible exposure, the strongest conclusion is {=follow credible guidance and seek testing or care when appropriate ~assume infection immediately ~blame the exposed person ~self-prescribe treatment}
